.SH NAME
mnnn\-spaces \- Code spaces: collections of code with a kind and a main (the entry point). Pipelines run spaces (`space:NAME`); main can call its members and other spaces
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmnnn spaces\fR [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-log\-file\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR] [\fB\-\-transport\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Code spaces: collections of code with a kind and a main (the entry point). Pipelines run spaces (`space:NAME`); main can call its members and other spaces
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Muninn home directory (default ~/.muninn)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Database file (default <home>/storage/muninn.database)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_DB\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR
Never prompt; missing values are errors
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_NON_INTERACTIVE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
More output (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Write logs to this file instead of stderr (the TUI defaults to <home>/logs/tui.log)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_LOG_FILE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print nothing but errors and requested data
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_QUIET\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Answer yes to every confirmation
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_YES\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR \fI<THEME_MODE>\fR
Override the theme mode for this run
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.IP \(bu 2
system
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_THEME_MODE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-transport\fR \fI<stream|poll>\fR
How live collaboration reaches peers: `stream` (gRPC streams, the default) or `poll` (requests over the peer connection; for containers). Overrides MUNINN_COLLAB_TRANSPORT and the `net config \-\-collab\-transport` setting
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH NOTES
.PP
A code space is a collection of code (`mnnn code`) with a kind (parser, transform, analysis,
ingest\-connector) and one main: the entry point that runs. Main can be plain code, or call
members (`host.call(ALIAS, frame)`) and whole other spaces (`host.call_space(NAME, frame)`),
declared in an `@imports a, b, space:NAME` header line. Only main calls; spaces calling spaces
can't loop and nest at most 8 deep.
.PP
Approving a space approves its line\-up (main, kind, members, aliases, pins, imported spaces).
Members follow their code: edits run at once, flagged unreviewed until the code is approved
(`mnnn code approve`). \-\-pin freezes a member at its current version; a pinned member that
changes fails until pinned again.
.PP
Examples:
  mnnn spaces create prices \-\-kind transform \-\-main parse\-csv \-\-add to\-bars
  mnnn spaces approve prices
  mnnn pipe \- space:prices model:bars < prices.csv
  mnnn spaces add prices clean\-rows \-\-as clean \-\-pin

.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
mnnn\-spaces\-export(1)
Write a code space file: the space, the spaces its main imports and every member\*(Aqs code (by trust hash). `\-` or no \-\-out: standard output
.TP
mnnn\-spaces\-import(1)
Import a code space file: shows the plan, then asks. Code and spaces land unapproved, pins kept; the same line\-up is reused, a clash lands as NAME\-imported
.TP
mnnn\-spaces\-list(1)
List code spaces: name, kind, main, members, approved, flags
.TP
mnnn\-spaces\-show(1)
A space: kind, main, members (pins, unreviewed edits), imports, approval
.TP
mnnn\-spaces\-create(1)
Create a space with MAIN as its main (not approved yet)
.TP
mnnn\-spaces\-add(1)
Add code to a space (followed; \-\-pin freezes it at its current version)
.TP
mnnn\-spaces\-remove\-code(1)
Take code out of a space (not its main)
.TP
mnnn\-spaces\-set\-main(1)
Make code (a member, or added now) the main
.TP
mnnn\-spaces\-pin(1)
Pin a member at its current version
.TP
mnnn\-spaces\-unpin(1)
Let a member follow its code again
.TP
mnnn\-spaces\-approve(1)
Approve a space\*(Aqs line\-up (and, asked, its unreviewed code)
.TP
mnnn\-spaces\-run(1)
Run a space (its main), over SOURCE if given
.TP
mnnn\-spaces\-rename(1)
Rename a space
.TP
mnnn\-spaces\-kind(1)
Change a space\*(Aqs kind
.TP
mnnn\-spaces\-enable(1)
.TP
mnnn\-spaces\-disable(1)
.TP
mnnn\-spaces\-remove(1)
Remove a space (its code stays; asks first)
